  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Purple’s showrooms delivered a third straight quarter of positive comparable sales, while e-commerce trends improved sequentially, pointing to recovering demand. The new premium Purple Royale line is gaining early traction at Mattress Firm, supporting wholesale momentum. However, total sales were modestly down, and the company’s failure to disclose quarterly revenue figures in its earnings release has created an information vacuum that unsettled investors, overshadowing the underlying operational progress.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** CEO Rob DeMartini emphasized consistency gains across channels and reaffirmed full-year EBITDA guidance, signaling confidence in a second-half trajectory. Yet the decision to withhold revenue data — even as EPS met expectations — has damaged transparency and market credibility, triggering a post-earnings share decline. The mixed execution reinforces a narrative of a turnaround that is making tentative operational strides while struggling to rebuild trust with the investment community.",
